    "fiftyone_vs_colmap": {
      "what_fiftyone_gives": "16,116 groups, each one turntable pose; each group has 4 slices (pos_1..pos_4) -- the 4 simultaneous camera exposures of that pose. plant_id, pose_id, pose_degrees, image_set_id and capture_datetime are per-sample fields, and 1,343 (plant, date) units contain the full 48 images.",
      "what_it_does_not_give": "no extrinsic camera poses and no COLMAP-style camera matrix per view. metadata.json carries no camera_intrinsics and no static_transforms (both empty), and the dataset card states the calibration npz files are not attached to samples. The only pose information is the nominal turntable angle (12 x 30 deg) and the 4 nominal camera elevations (45/90/135/180 deg).",
      "consequence_for_reconstruction": "a capture unit is reconstructable in principle -- 48 views of one plant on a known turntable, with known intrinsics -- but the camera motion must be either recovered by SfM on the images or derived from the nominal angles, and the white backdrop/pot must be masked out or SfM will lock onto it. Neither is established by the metadata alone.",
      "joinability": "the macro-photograph segmentation subset is a different imaging task (different camera, different window, no plant_id/pose/session ids) and must not be joined to the rig images by plant id."
    }
  },
